  "score_conversion": "No automatic conversion. Rate every unified criterion directly from the complete item. The crosswalk identifies related concepts, not score equivalence or an averaging rule.",
  "comparability_note": "Chemistry uses a direct family mapping. Legal harmonization merges separately scored concepts in some templates and applies common quality checks in every item, changing weighting and coverage. Identical /40 ranges do not establish equivalence to historical verifier totals. Type compliance is intentionally outside the public annotation task.",
  "public_presentation": "One genuine example document appears before the eight plain-language checks, each followed by its unified criterion name in parentheses. Each criterion paragraph begins with a definition, then gives judging and scoring instructions. Each check has Good and Bad question–answer examples, each followed by a suggested 1–5 score and a brief explanation for that criterion only. Saved generated examples are preferred; teaching edits or new examples are allowed when no suitable saved example exists. No faithfulness/quality group labels, question-type taxonomy, or separate verdict/evidence fields are shown. A fourth page tests understanding of the annotation task and scoring instructions through 10 single-choice questions, each with four options and one correct answer. The expected answers and readiness rule are kept in coordinator files.",
